   $q$Why does Grandma Ines say nothing when Mateo plants the beans too deep?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She wants Mateo to fail so that he will stop visiting the garden.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"She wants him to find the mistake himself so he will be ready to learn.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She thinks the beans will grow well no matter how deep they are.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She does not notice the mistake because she is busy humming.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She wants him to find the mistake himself so he will be ready to learn.$q$, $q$She says that when the beans do not come up, "he will finally be ready to listen." She clearly notices the mistake, since she describes it, so she is not too busy to see it.$q$, 'draft', '54757fb5-2297-5585-970f-f9c0d88d28be')
