   $q$What does the Otter mean when she says, "It seems we were both half right"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Neither animal had any good ideas, so both should change completely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"They will split the dam in half so each can live in one part.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Each view had value, but each needed the other to be complete.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The Beaver was fully right, and the Otter is only being polite.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each view had value, but each needed the other to be complete.$q$, $q$The Beaver's planning built the lodge that sheltered her, and her swimming saved the dam, so each point of view was partly correct. Both views proved useful, so it is wrong to say neither had good ideas.$q$, 'draft', '5082df26-dd15-56b6-9671-375964d93845')
