   $q$Near the end, the voices trade single lines ("I take one step." / "I look up."). What effect does this structure create?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that the speakers have stopped noticing each other.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"It speeds up the poem and pulls the two speakers closer together.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It slows the poem so the reader can rest before a new topic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It shows the two speakers are arguing about who gets the seat.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It speeds up the poem and pulls the two speakers closer together.$q$, $q$The stanzas shrink to one line each, so the voices answer each other quickly as Amara and Jun move toward meeting. They are noticing each other, not ignoring each other, and they never argue.$q$, 'draft', '4bc3369d-db84-55bf-aff4-d38787677868')
